76. BeanFactory:

Basic Spring IoC container for creating and managing beans.

77. ApplicationContext:

Advanced IoC container that extends BeanFactory and provides additional Spring features.

78. Difference:

BeanFactory provides basic bean management; ApplicationContext provides bean management plus additional enterprise/application features.

79. Lazy loading:

Bean is created only when it is needed/requested.

80. Eager loading:

Bean is created during application startup.

81. Why ApplicationContext?

Because it provides additional features such as events, i18n, resource loading, and better Spring integration.

82. Types:

ClassPathXmlApplicationContext, FileSystemXmlApplicationContext, AnnotationConfigApplicationContext, and web-oriented ApplicationContext
implementations.















